Package: mouse-options
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyqt6, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-pyudev, python3-evdev,
 python3-xlib, python3-yaml, libxkbcommon0, libxcb-cursor0, systemd
Recommends: wireplumber | pulseaudio-utils
Maintainer: Walbert Freitas <217115970+walbertfreitas@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Configure Logitech mouse buttons easily, like Options+
 Mouse Options is a simple, visual way to configure Logitech mice on Linux:
 click a button on the picture of the mouse and pick what it should do
 (media, editing, windows, browser, keyboard shortcuts, open apps), set
 gestures on the gesture button and use different settings per application.
 It has its own HID++ service (no Solaar needed): changes apply instantly,
 actions avoid simulated keystrokes whenever a direct way exists, and the
 configuration is re-applied when the mouse reconnects. Interface in English
 and Portuguese.
 .
 Independent project; not affiliated with or endorsed by Logitech.
